I am standing by my apartment.
I have a bag with a cinnamon pastry.
My neighbour Nina is at the door.
She smiles broadly and says hello.
"Hello Maya, do you have a Danish number now?" Nina asks.
"Yes, I have a new phone number," I reply.
"That is good," she says.
I have my phone in my hand.
"What is your number?" I ask.
"My number is eighty-seven, sixty-five, forty-three, twenty-one," Nina says.
I write her number on my phone.
"And my number is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight," I say.
Nina saves my number on her phone.
Now we have contact.
We go inside together.
I am very happy about my new friend.
